      "evidence": "A live payment secret key is hardcoded in source and committed to git. src/config.js exports `paymentApiKey: 'sk_live_51N0TAREALSECRET'` and `git log -S 'sk_live_51N0TAREALSECRET' --all` confirms it is tracked in history (commit '194cf1c task baseline'). The `sk_live_` prefix denotes a production/payment live credential and the value is read into a module-level constant with no env-var indirection, so anyone with repo read access obtains the secret. A leaked live payment key allows charging cards, issuing refunds, and accessing payment-platform customer data (direct financial impact).",
      "remediation": "Remove the hardcoded value from source and purge it from git history (BFG / git filter-repo, then force-push). Rotate/revoke the key at the payment provider immediately. Load the credential from a secret manager or environment variable (e.g. `paymentApiKey: process.env.PAYMENT_API_KEY`) and fail fast if unset. Add `config.js` secrets to `.gitignore` if it ever holds local values."
    },
    {
      "category": "open-redirect",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "files": ["src/redirect.js"],
      "evidence": "User-controlled input reaches a redirect sink with no validation. `continueTo(req, res)` calls `res.redirect(req.query.next)` directly: the entire `next` query parameter is used as the redirect target with no allowlist, same-origin check, or relative-path restriction. Express `res.redirect()` honors absolute external URLs, so a request to the route with `?next=https://evil.com` returns `302 Location: https://evil.com`. This is exploitable for phishing via trusted-domain links and for redirect_uri/OAuth token-theft chaining.",
      "remediation": "Validate the redirect target before redirecting: only allow known-safe destinations (allowlist) or require relative same-origin paths. For example, reject non-relative URLs and verify the resolved path stays within the app: `const next = req.query.next || '/'; if (!next.startsWith('/') || next.startsWith('//')) return res.status(400).end(); res.redirect(next);`. Do not pass raw external user input to `res.redirect()`."
    }
  ],
  "scanned_files": ["src/config.js", "src/health.js", "src/redirect.js"],
  "source_modified": false
}
"}

